-- title:
--   Decomposition-group equivariance of the pinned function field embedding
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ denotes the completion `A₁.valuation.Completion` of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ at the valuation subring $A_1$, $\mathcal{X}_C$ denotes the fibre product of $f_0 : \mathcal{X}_0 \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the composite $\mathcal{O}_0 \to$ `ratClosure A₁` $\to \mathbb{C}_{q'}$, and $X_C$ denotes the fibre product of $\pi_X$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \mathbb{C}_{q'}$ followed by `sbar`.
--
--   The data are as follows.
--
--   *Numerical data.* A non-zero natural number $N$ that is squarefree, primes $q$ and $q'$ with $q' \ne q$, neither dividing $N$, both at least $5$, and a non-zero natural number $D$ divisible by $2Nqq'$.
--
--   *The place above $q'$.* A valuation subring $A_1$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A₁.LiesOverPrime q'`, i.e. $q'$ lies in the non-units of $A_1$; the hypothesis `hiso₁` that every element of the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ preserves `A₁.valuation`; and a height-one prime $v_1$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q' \in v_1$.
--
--   *Definite quaternion data at $q$.* Rationals $a_2, b_2$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt q`, i.e. $a_2 < 0$, $b_2 < 0$ and, for each finite place $v$ of $\mathbb{Q}$, the completion $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_2,b_2] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q \in v$; a maximal order $\Lambda_2$ and an Eichler order $R_2$ of level $N$ (that is, an intersection of two maximal orders of relative index $N$) with $R_2 \le \Lambda_2$; a finite-idelic unit $n_2$ in `primeHeckeSet R₂ q'`; the hypotheses that `meetOrder R₂ n₂` $= R_2 \cap n_2 R_2 n_2^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nq'$, that conjugation of this order by $n_2$ returns it, and that the shift by $n_2$ on the class set of its finite-idelic stabiliser is an involution; finiteness and decidability instances for the relevant class sets; and `hlaws₂`, the predicate `ClassSetHeckeLaws N q' Λ₂ R₂ n₂` (four clauses: the edge Hecke matrices commute with one another, the vertex Hecke matrices commute with one another, the two degeneracy pushforwards intertwine edge and vertex Hecke operators at primes other than $q$, and the joint kernel of the degeneracy maps is stable under the edge Hecke operators).
--
--   *Indefinite quaternion data.* Rationals $a, b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q q'`, i.e. $0 < a$ or $0 < b$ and the completion at a finite place $v$ is a division algebra exactly when $q \in v$ or $q' \in v$; and a maximal order $\Lambda$ in $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$.
--
--   *Coarse moduli over the $D$-integers.* A field `Fbar` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ which is a curve in the sense of `IsCurveOver` (principal divisors of degree zero exist, residue fields of places are finite over the base, and the module of Kähler differentials is free of rank one) and essentially of finite type; a scheme $X$ with a morphism $\pi_X$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `Localization.Away ((D : ℕ) : ℤ)`, a point `sbar` of that base with values in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and an assignment `pt` sending a fake elliptic curve of level $N$ for $\Lambda$ over a commutative ring $S$ and a base point $s$ to a point of $X$ over $s$; together with the four moduli axioms `pt_iso`, `pt_pullback`, `pt_surjective`, `pt_injective` (invariance under isomorphism of fake elliptic curves, compatibility with base change along a ring homomorphism and pullback of fake elliptic curves, and bijectivity on isomorphism classes over algebraically closed fields).
--
--   *Curve model and Hecke tower.* A `CurveModel` $\mathfrak{M}$ for $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq$ `Fbar`, an isomorphism $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$ from $\mathfrak{M}.C$ to the fibre product of $\pi_X$ and `sbar` compatible with the structure morphisms to $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a homomorphism `gal` from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to the semilinear automorphisms of `Fbar` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, tower data $\mathbb{T}$ for the primes away from $q, q'$ with Galois actions `galT` and involutions $W$, `WT`, and a witness `tw` of type `ModuliTowerWitnessD` relating these to `pt`, `sbar` and $\mathfrak{M}$.
--
--   *The $q'$-adic matrix embedding.* An injective $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra map $\iota_1$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_2,b_2]$ into $2 \times 2$ matrices over the subfield [`ValuationSubring.ratClosure A₁`](def/ValuationSubring_CompletionRatClosure.html#L13) of $\mathbb{C}_{q'}$, the induced projective representation $\rho_1$ of the unit group together with the identity `hρ₁` expressing $\rho_1$ as the class of $\iota_1$, a pseudo-uniformiser $\varpi_1$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ is $q'$, and the hypothesis that the ring of holomorphic functions `HolRingOf ϖ₁ ρ₁` is a domain.
--
--   *Hecke elements, groups and Atkin–Lehner elements.* For each prime $\ell$ distinct from $q$ and $q'$, a quaternion unit $s_1(\ell)$ and a finite-idelic unit $sf_1(\ell)$ subject to `hs₁` (four clauses: the component of $sf_1(\ell)$ at each place not above $q'$ is $s_1(\ell) \otimes 1$, the component at the places above $q'$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_1(\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₂ (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₂ n₂) ℓ` otherwise, and the reduced norm of $s_1(\ell)$ is $\ell$); subgroups $\Gamma_1$ indexed by `Option` of these primes, with $\Gamma_1(\mathrm{none})$ the group of units lying in `awayUnits R₂ v₁` whose reduced norm has even $q'$-adic valuation, and $\Gamma_1(\ell)$ its intersection with its conjugate by $s_1(\ell)$; elements $w_1$ of reduced norm $q'$, lying in `awayUnits R₂ v₁` at the base and in `awayUnits (meetOrder R₂ (sf₁ ℓ)) v₁` at each $\ell$; and elements $\bar{w}_1$ of reduced norm $q$ whose local behaviour is prescribed by `hwbar₁`: at every place $u \ne v_1$ not above $q$ the local image lies in the unit box of the relevant order, and at every place $u \ne v_1$ conjugation by it preserves the local boxes of the relevant order and of $\Lambda_2$ (the relevant order being $R_2$ at the base and `meetOrder R₂ (sf₁ ℓ)` at each $\ell$).
--
--   *Decomposition action and quadratic character.* A homomorphism $dIso_1$ from the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ to the isometric automorphisms of $\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ over `ratClosure A₁`, whose underlying ring equivalence is the Galois action ($dIso_1(\tau)(x) = \tau \cdot x$); and a character $\chi$ of the decomposition subgroup with values in $\mathrm{Multiplicative}(\mathbb{Z}/2)$ which is trivial on inertia, non-trivial on every Frobenius at $q'$, and satisfies $\chi(\tau) = 1$ if and only if $\tau$ fixes every element $x$ of the residue field of $A_1$ with $x^{q'^2} = x$.
--
--   *Coefficient rings.* A characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}_0$ with irreducible element $\pi$, $\pi$-adically complete, with residue field of cardinality $q'$ and $(q') = (\pi)$, which is an $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra inside `ratClosure A₁` with the latter as fraction field; a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal{O}_{nr}$ over $\mathcal{O}_0$ with an $\mathcal{O}_0$-automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, with that ideal maximal, every element integral modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x) \equiv x^{q'}$ modulo $\pi$; a homomorphism $vdet$ recording the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant, characterised by `hvdet`; a ring homomorphism $\psi_0 : \mathcal{O}_{nr} \to \mathbb{C}_{q'}$ with values of valuation at most $1$ and compatible with $\mathcal{O}_0$; the identifications $\pi = \varpi_1.\varpi$, the invertibility of $N$ in $\mathcal{O}_0$, the characterisation of the image of $\mathcal{O}_0$ in `ratClosure A₁` as the elements of valuation at most $1$; and `hrk`, stating that for $x$ of valuation less than $1$ and $y \ne 0$ some power of the valuation of $x$ is at most the valuation of $y$.
--
--   *Integral models and correspondences over $\mathcal{O}_0$.* A scheme $\mathcal{X}_0$ with structure morphism $f_0$ and a moduli assignment $pt_0$ satisfying `IsCoarseModuli Λ N` (the four axioms above plus the universal property), with $\mathcal{X}_0$ integral and $f_0$ flat, separated, locally of finite type and quasi-compact; for each prime $\ell$ away from $q'$ and $q$, a scheme $\mathcal{Y}_0(\ell)$ with structure morphism $g_0(\ell)$ and assignment $ptT_0(\ell)$ satisfying `IsCoarseModuliT Λ N ℓ`; two degeneracy morphisms $d_{00}(\ell), d_{10}(\ell) : \mathcal{Y}_0(\ell) \to \mathcal{X}_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$, the first taking the moduli point of a curve with extra level-$\ell$ structure to the moduli point of the underlying curve and the second to the moduli point of the target of a level-$\ell$ isogeny; and endomorphisms $ar$, $\overline{ar}$ of $\mathcal{X}_0$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal{O}_0$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $q'$ and at $q$ on moduli points.
--
--   *Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation.* Natural families $\Theta$ and $\Theta_T(\ell)$ from the product of the functor corepresented by $\mathcal{O}_{nr}$ with the Deligne-datum functor `FormalOmega.Omega (ratClosure A₁) π` to the nilpotent points of $f_0$, respectively of $g_0(\ell)$; and `hCD` (twelve clauses, summarised here): naturality of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta_T(\ell)$; invariance of $\Theta$ under the twisted action `FormalOmega.OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` of the image under $\iota_1$ of any $\gamma \in$ `awayUnits R₂ v₁`, and of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ under that of $\gamma$ in the intersection of `awayUnits R₂ v₁` with its conjugate by $s_1(\ell)$; over an algebraically closed field in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and for each $\mathcal{O}_0$-algebra map $\psi$ from $\mathcal{O}_{nr}$, surjectivity of $\Theta$ (respectively $\Theta_T(\ell)$) in the second variable together with the identification of its fibres as the orbits of the twisted action of the corresponding group; the universal property of $\Theta$ and of each $\Theta_T(\ell)$ among such invariant natural families, with uniqueness; the compatibility of $\Theta_T(\ell)$ with $d_{00}(\ell)$ and, through the twisted action of $s_1(\ell)$, with $d_{10}(\ell)$; and the compatibility of $\Theta$ with $ar$ through the Frobenius twist by $1$ on the $\mathcal{O}_{nr}$-component and with $\overline{ar}$ through the twisted action of $\bar{w}_1(\mathrm{none})$. Both $\mathcal{X}_C$ and each base change of $g_0(\ell)$ to $\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ are assumed integral.
--
--   *Comparison isomorphism and pinned embedding.* An isomorphism $u$ from $X_C$ to $\mathcal{X}_C$ commuting with the projections to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ and compatible with the two moduli assignments `pt` and $pt_0$ in the sense of `hupt`; and a ring homomorphism $j$ from `Fbar` to the function field of $\mathcal{X}_C$ pinned by `hpin`: for every $x \in$ `Fbar`, every open $U$ of $\mathfrak{M}.C$ containing its generic point, every witness that the generic point of $\mathcal{X}_C$ lies in the preimage of $U$ under the comparison morphism $\mathcal{X}_C \to \mathfrak{M}.C$ obtained from $u^{-1}$, the canonical lift of the projections of $X_C$ and the inverse of $e_{\mathfrak{M}}$, and every section over $U$ whose germ at the generic point of $\mathfrak{M}.C$ is $\mathfrak{M}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}(x)$, the germ at the generic point of $\mathcal{X}_C$ of the pullback of that section equals $j(x)$.
--
--   *Conclusion.* For every $\tau$ in the decomposition subgroup of $A_1$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and every endomorphism $t_C$ of $\mathcal{X}_C$ such that $t_C$ followed by the first projection to $\mathcal{X}_0$ equals that projection, and $t_C$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ equals that projection followed by $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring automorphism underlying $dIso_1(\tau)$, the following holds: for every $x \in$ `Fbar`, every open $U$ of $\mathcal{X}_C$ containing its generic point, every witness that the generic point lies in $t_C^{-1}U$, and every section `sec` of the structure sheaf over $U$ whose germ at the generic point equals $j(x)$, the germ at the generic point of the section $(t_C)^{*}\mathrm{sec}$ over $t_C^{-1}U$ equals $j(\mathrm{gal}(\tau) \cdot x)$, where $\tau$ is regarded as an element of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ through the inclusion of the decomposition subgroup and the action is that of the semilinear automorphism $\mathrm{gal}(\tau)$ on `Fbar`.
--
--   This is the equivariance statement for the function-field embedding $j$ of the Shimura-curve model into the $q'$-adically completed integral model: any lift to $\mathcal{X}_C$ of the $\tau$-action on $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{C}_{q'}$ over the identity of $\mathcal{X}_0$ acts on germs at the generic point through the Galois action $\mathrm{gal}(\tau)$ on the function field. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_of_iso_pullback_completion_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.exists_ringHom_functionField_of_iso_pullback_completion_one_zero_of_two_mul_dvd) in the comparison of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation with the curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$.
